Z||000000||Fleabitdog||05-22-2001||12:59 AM||||Are all 88 hub and bearings the same? I beleive the only difference in the front suspension on the 88's is the springs, but I just want to be sure. Thanks  Dave||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-22-2001||03:03 AM||||The '88 front wheel bearings/hubs are different from the rears and are unique only to '88s (all '84-'88 rear wheel bearings are the same).<P>As far as differences in fronts suspensions......the entire suspension is different from the earlier years.  I think you know this and are asking about the differences between '88 models (coupe, Formula & GT)......in that respect, yes....the only real difference is spring rates.  The coupe has a softer spring rating than the Formula/GT.  I also believe the shock valving was different, but that's a moot point now since the original shocks have likely been replaced by now on most Fieros.<P>I hope I answered your question.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fleabitdog||05-22-2001||09:02 AM||||Thanks Mike. That is what i meant. I know a person that needs a front hub and bearing for a formula and just wanted to be sure.  dave||||reg||1
